## 2.7. Examples of algebras
%%%
tag := "Chapter2/Discussion_2.7_intro/heading-1"
%%%

The following two examples are among the simplest interesting examples of noncommutative associative algebras:

(1) the **Weyl algebra**, $`k\langle x, y \rangle / \langle yx - xy - 1 \rangle`;

(2) the **$`q`-Weyl algebra**, generated by $`x, x^{-1}, y, y^{-1}` with defining relations $`yx = qxy` and $`xx^{-1} = x^{-1}x = yy^{-1} = y^{-1}y = 1`.
